 "messages": [
  {
   "role": "designer",
   "text": "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N8 board with USB-C 5 V input and protected native USB, AP2112K 3.3 V regulator, BOOT/RESET buttons and a 3.3 V JST-SH I2C sensor connector. External sensor allowance 50 mA. Requires a known 5 V Type-C source advertising at least 1.5 A. Software checks pass with thermal/transient an"
  },
  {
   "role": "fixer",
   "text": "Schematic gate failed, so nothing was built. SPICE spice-unavailable: Unsupported actual R value on R1 The failure is a SPICE value-parser incompatibility in an existing library block: esp32-s3-core R1 has value '10kOhm'. I independently checked the ESP32-S3-WROOM datasheet page 41: it explicitly recommends 10 kOhm and 1 uF at EN, so the electrical value is correct. Other existing library resistors use the same unit-suffixed notation. The bounded technical fix would be to normalize these value strings to numeric ohms without changing components or wiring. However, all affected library blocks e"
  }
 ],
